1
00:00:37,162 --> 00:00:39,789
Mikoy and Chiara are living
the best years of their lives.

2
00:00:39,873 --> 00:00:42,584
<i>And now they finally have the chance</i>
<i>to live a normal life</i>

3
00:00:42,667 --> 00:00:43,501
<i>and be truly happy.</i>

4
00:00:43,585 --> 00:00:46,045
<i>So I'm sure that every moment,</i>

5
00:00:46,129 --> 00:00:47,172
<i>they're incredibly happy</i>

6
00:00:47,255 --> 00:00:48,840
<i>and surrounded by love.</i>

7
00:00:48,923 --> 00:00:51,134
<i>But honestly, Mom, I'm still upset.</i>

8
00:00:51,217 --> 00:00:53,178
This is the life we dreamed of.

9
00:00:53,261 --> 00:00:54,846
<i>It feels like she's sabotaging it.</i>

10
00:00:54,929 --> 00:00:57,682
Is the life I'm offering her
really too simple?

11
00:00:57,766 --> 00:01:00,185
Instead of asking me that,

12
00:01:00,268 --> 00:01:01,978
why don't you ask her yourself?

13
00:01:03,271 --> 00:01:06,232
<i>Chiara and Sir Pandoy</i>
<i>already talked the other day.</i>

14
00:01:06,316 --> 00:01:08,735
<i>Yes, Chiara went to see him.</i>

15
00:01:08,818 --> 00:01:10,195
<i>She already apologized.</i>

16
00:01:10,278 --> 00:01:12,197
And he gave her another chance.

17
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:14,365
Mikoy, you said it yourself, right?

18
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:16,493
This is Chiara's first time
living this kind of life.

19
00:01:16,576 --> 00:01:19,079
<i>You know, I really admire Chiara.</i>

20
00:01:19,162 --> 00:01:21,998
I'm sure she'll go far in this business.

21
00:01:28,880 --> 00:01:34,052
I'll be with you
until my very last breath.

22
00:01:42,143 --> 00:01:44,979
Here's to Mikoy and Chiara,
the future bride and groom!

23
00:01:48,399 --> 00:01:50,151
The hot soup's on me!

24
00:01:54,114 --> 00:01:56,533
And here's another toast

25
00:01:56,616 --> 00:01:58,868
to the little ones who will

26
00:01:58,952 --> 00:02:02,705
carry on the Pinagpala legacy!

27
00:02:02,789 --> 00:02:05,083
- Pinagpala!
- Cheers!

28
00:02:05,166 --> 00:02:08,378
Honey, don't put
so much pressure on the kids.

29
00:02:08,461 --> 00:02:09,462
They're just getting started.

30
00:02:09,546 --> 00:02:12,006
Oh, come on. You.

31
00:02:13,341 --> 00:02:14,759
Looks like Angelito wants

32
00:02:14,843 --> 00:02:16,845
to say something too. Come on, everyone.

33
00:02:21,516 --> 00:02:25,770
<i>I just want to say I'm so, so happy.</i>

34
00:02:28,148 --> 00:02:33,111
<i>I really appreciate all of</i>
<i>Mikoy's sacrifices.</i>

35
00:02:33,862 --> 00:02:35,155
Even though

36
00:02:36,489 --> 00:02:38,533
he always tells me

37
00:02:39,409 --> 00:02:40,869
not to worry.

38
00:02:41,953 --> 00:02:43,037
But…

39
00:02:45,331 --> 00:02:47,709
I can't help blaming myself.

40
00:02:50,211 --> 00:02:52,338
<i>I always blame myself because…</i>

41
00:02:55,049 --> 00:02:58,136
If it weren't for me, maybe…

42
00:02:59,929 --> 00:03:02,015
Mikoy wouldn't have
had to go through all those

43
00:03:02,098 --> 00:03:03,266
complicated situations.

44
00:03:05,268 --> 00:03:07,812
<i>So, today…</i>

45
00:03:14,777 --> 00:03:16,154
<i>I'm so, so happy.</i>

46
00:03:19,198 --> 00:03:20,825
<i>I'm so happy that</i>

47
00:03:22,285 --> 00:03:27,290
<i>Mikoy has finally found</i>
<i>his happily ever after.</i>

48
00:03:29,834 --> 00:03:32,170
<i>Chiara, Mikoy.</i>

49
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:39,260
<i>I'm truly happy for both of you.</i>

50
00:03:43,097 --> 00:03:45,558
I'll always be here to support

51
00:03:46,059 --> 00:03:49,354
this new chapter in your love story.

52
00:03:56,444 --> 00:03:59,155
- That was so sweet.
- Angelito.

53
00:03:59,239 --> 00:04:00,114
Angelito!

54
00:04:00,949 --> 00:04:03,243
I'm just really, really happy.

55
00:04:03,993 --> 00:04:06,120
Angelito, your face isn't moving.

56
00:04:06,704 --> 00:04:08,331
- Oh, gosh.
- Angelito, can you hear us?

57
00:04:08,414 --> 00:04:11,251
Your signal's probably weak,
that's why it's lagging.

58
00:04:12,585 --> 00:04:14,420
Is that so?

59
00:04:14,504 --> 00:04:15,338
- Son.
- It's okay, honey.

60
00:04:15,421 --> 00:04:17,632
Whatever Angelito was going to say,
I'm sure it was something wonderful.

61
00:04:17,715 --> 00:04:20,260
- That’s for sure!
- For sure.

62
00:04:20,343 --> 00:04:22,553
What a shame. It sounded like
he still had a lot more to say.

63
00:04:22,637 --> 00:04:23,846
That's enough.

64
00:04:23,930 --> 00:04:25,223
- Okay, you can hang up now.
- Forget about it.

65
00:04:25,306 --> 00:04:26,849
Must be the weak signal.

66
00:04:26,933 --> 00:04:28,893
Chiara! How about a speech?

67
00:04:28,977 --> 00:04:33,898
- Chiara!
- Yes.

68
00:04:47,078 --> 00:04:48,579
Good afternoon, Senator Quintin.

69
00:04:56,963 --> 00:04:58,673
May we talk?

70
00:05:01,801 --> 00:05:04,012
Just the two of us?

71
00:05:08,224 --> 00:05:09,851
Just the two of us.

72
00:05:11,519 --> 00:05:12,729
I'll just use the restroom.

73
00:05:19,444 --> 00:05:21,404
How may I help you?

74
00:05:25,283 --> 00:05:30,997
Are you really okay with Mikoy and Chiara
moving around freely,

75
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:34,917
without anyone keeping an eye on them?

76
00:05:35,585 --> 00:05:37,754
As far as this agency is concerned,

77
00:05:38,504 --> 00:05:40,757
Mikoy and Chiara have already
fulfilled their responsibilities.

78
00:05:41,340 --> 00:05:44,635
They're free to live however they choose.

79
00:05:45,595 --> 00:05:48,806
But you said it yourself,

80
00:05:48,890 --> 00:05:51,017
Mikoy is a very valuable asset.

81
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:53,978
He can adapt to any situation.

82
00:05:54,687 --> 00:05:56,939
And after everything he's been through,

83
00:05:57,440 --> 00:06:01,736
he's trained well enough
to excel in combat.

84
00:06:02,236 --> 00:06:07,450
And if you pair him with Chiara,

85
00:06:08,159 --> 00:06:12,455
you'll have an incredibly powerful duo.

86
00:06:13,581 --> 00:06:17,627
But I don't think they'd want
to return and serve the agency again.

87
00:06:31,682 --> 00:06:32,809
But knowing them,

88
00:06:33,309 --> 00:06:36,813
I can't imagine them returning
to such a dangerous and complicated life.

89
00:06:38,272 --> 00:06:42,193
What if we had some leverage?

90
00:06:43,152 --> 00:06:45,905
Let's use Chiara's parents.

91
00:06:45,988 --> 00:06:50,701
Mr. Viktor and Mrs. Donabel Valtrovi.

92
00:06:53,871 --> 00:06:55,164
In exchange,

93
00:06:55,248 --> 00:07:01,629
we can set free the people
who matter most to Chiara.

94
00:07:08,719 --> 00:07:11,222
- Chiara!
- There she is.

95
00:07:11,305 --> 00:07:13,224
I'll indulge Dekyo this time.

96
00:07:13,307 --> 00:07:16,436
But I'm starting to worry
about your liver.

97
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:20,189
Thank you.

98
00:07:21,858 --> 00:07:25,736
Honestly, I still feel like
I'm floating on cloud nine.

99
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:33,786
It's just…

100
00:07:41,711 --> 00:07:43,254
I've been feeling

101
00:07:43,963 --> 00:07:45,381
terrified.

102
00:07:46,340 --> 00:07:49,469
As you all know,

103
00:07:49,552 --> 00:07:53,431
both of my parents are in prison.

104
00:07:53,931 --> 00:07:57,935
So I started thinking,
"What if I end up alone forever?"

105
00:07:58,019 --> 00:08:02,732
And on top of that,
this community is still so new to me.

106
00:08:03,941 --> 00:08:06,736
Not just for me, but for all of us.

107
00:08:07,612 --> 00:08:10,531
Especially for me because it's

108
00:08:10,615 --> 00:08:13,701
so different from the life I grew up in.

109
00:08:13,784 --> 00:08:15,077
Back in Prague.

110
00:08:15,870 --> 00:08:18,623
And I was just afraid that

111
00:08:20,082 --> 00:08:21,834
when I woke up,

112
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:24,754
none of you would be there anymore.

113
00:08:28,508 --> 00:08:30,134
To Mom Tess

114
00:08:32,094 --> 00:08:33,763
and Dad Mario,

115
00:08:34,472 --> 00:08:37,808
despite everything my family has done,

116
00:08:39,101 --> 00:08:41,646
you still welcomed me with open arms.

117
00:08:43,606 --> 00:08:45,024
Thank you.

118
00:08:45,525 --> 00:08:48,945
Thank you for your love and appreciation.

119
00:08:50,530 --> 00:08:53,491
Thank you for still accepting me
as your son's partner.

120
00:08:56,869 --> 00:09:00,414
And to all you crazy bunch…

121
00:09:01,791 --> 00:09:03,125
Oh my.

122
00:09:03,209 --> 00:09:08,172
Somehow, I've accepted that
you'll all be part of my life forever.

123
00:09:11,509 --> 00:09:13,511
And even you, Rahmboy,

124
00:09:13,594 --> 00:09:17,181
who popped into our lives
out of nowhere like a mushroom.

125
00:09:18,099 --> 00:09:18,933
A mushroom.

126
00:09:19,976 --> 00:09:21,978
And of course,

127
00:09:22,061 --> 00:09:24,564
to the love of my life.

128
00:09:27,733 --> 00:09:30,653
And to the bonds I've built
with all of you.

129
00:09:31,362 --> 00:09:34,657
For the first time in my life,
I felt fear.

130
00:09:36,742 --> 00:09:40,663
Chiara Valtrovi isn't someone
who gets scared.

131
00:09:42,540 --> 00:09:44,500
But I've realized it's okay to be afraid.

132
00:09:45,501 --> 00:09:47,420
It's okay to carry fear in your heart.

133
00:09:48,170 --> 00:09:51,299
Because that means it's full.

134
00:09:51,382 --> 00:09:54,510
It means I finally have people
I'm afraid of losing.

135
00:09:56,887 --> 00:09:57,972
I hope

136
00:09:59,724 --> 00:10:01,350
you'll never get tired of me.

137
00:10:01,434 --> 00:10:03,686
Of course not!

138
00:10:03,769 --> 00:10:06,606
Even if I can be scary sometimes.

139
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:14,947
So…

140
00:10:17,158 --> 00:10:20,453
I'm truly grateful that you accepted me.

141
00:10:26,584 --> 00:10:27,585
So…

142
00:10:56,781 --> 00:10:57,615
Bok?

143
00:10:59,742 --> 00:11:00,660
Hey!

144
00:11:03,287 --> 00:11:04,288
Bok.

145
00:11:04,372 --> 00:11:07,833
I was just looking for a place to eat.
Thought I'd treat myself.

146
00:11:07,917 --> 00:11:09,377
You know, after La Morte Bianca,

147
00:11:09,460 --> 00:11:11,170
I've got mountains of paperwork
to deal with.

148
00:11:11,253 --> 00:11:12,671
It's as high as Mayon Volcano.

149
00:11:12,755 --> 00:11:14,298
Well, you know,

150
00:11:14,382 --> 00:11:17,760
government work always comes
with endless paperwork.

151
00:11:19,011 --> 00:11:20,596
What about you? What are you doing here?

152
00:11:22,681 --> 00:11:24,141
Wait.

153
00:11:24,225 --> 00:11:25,726
Don't tell me you're on a date?

154
00:11:28,771 --> 00:11:31,399
I'm sure you don't have time for romance.

155
00:11:34,318 --> 00:11:36,487
Sir Quintin talked to me.

156
00:11:41,409 --> 00:11:45,496
Well, he knows,
and we both know, they won't agree.

157
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:48,499
That's exactly what I told him,
but he won't let it go.

158
00:11:48,582 --> 00:11:52,169
He wants us to use Donabel and Viktor
as leverage.

159
00:11:55,506 --> 00:11:58,509
I already told him that,
but he keeps insisting.

160
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:01,262
He thinks that since
we managed to integrate

161
00:12:01,345 --> 00:12:03,097
Cocoy and Carlota into the agency,

162
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:06,016
we can do the same with Mikoy and Chiara.

163
00:12:11,814 --> 00:12:15,443
But what we need to remind
the Senator is that

164
00:12:15,526 --> 00:12:17,695
we are a law enforcement agency.

165
00:12:17,778 --> 00:12:19,238
We're not a kill squad.

166
00:12:20,197 --> 00:12:21,574
- That's exactly what I said.
- Okay?

167
00:12:21,657 --> 00:12:23,159
But he just won't budge.

168
00:12:23,742 --> 00:12:24,702
Exactly.

169
00:12:29,874 --> 00:12:31,250
Are you wearing cologne?

170
00:12:32,918 --> 00:12:34,795
- No, I always do.
- Wait a second.

171
00:12:35,504 --> 00:12:37,882
Seriously, are you really on a date?

172
00:12:40,134 --> 00:12:42,094
Bok, you know…

173
00:12:42,178 --> 00:12:43,387
To be honest…

174
00:12:44,054 --> 00:12:47,516
I started seeing someone.

175
00:12:52,354 --> 00:12:54,690
I've been looking for the right time
to tell you,

176
00:12:54,773 --> 00:12:57,651
but you happened to find me here.

177
00:12:58,360 --> 00:13:00,738
Wait… Who is it? Do I know her?

178
00:13:13,334 --> 00:13:14,335
Alex!

179
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:16,754
Bok.

180
00:13:27,598 --> 00:13:32,394
Mom Tess!

181
00:13:32,478 --> 00:13:36,023
Mom Tess!

182
00:13:38,025 --> 00:13:43,364
Chiara!

183
00:13:43,447 --> 00:13:46,825
Chiara!

184
00:13:46,909 --> 00:13:50,621
Chiara!

185
00:13:50,704 --> 00:13:56,502
Rahmboy!

186
00:14:02,258 --> 00:14:03,801
Your mom is something else.

187
00:14:08,389 --> 00:14:10,891
Hang on, Dad. Want to join the dancing?

188
00:14:10,975 --> 00:14:13,644
You've got the best dance moves!

189
00:14:14,270 --> 00:14:16,730
Just me? Both of us!

190
00:14:18,983 --> 00:14:20,943
That's right!

191
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:31,537
You know, son?

192
00:14:33,539 --> 00:14:35,416
I'm so proud of you.

193
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:40,588
Proud of me?

194
00:14:43,090 --> 00:14:44,800
Have I really done anything right?

195
00:14:46,218 --> 00:14:47,303
There you go again.

196
00:14:48,262 --> 00:14:49,763
Always selling yourself short.

197
00:14:51,849 --> 00:14:53,100
But I admit.

198
00:14:53,809 --> 00:14:55,311
There were times I wondered…

199
00:14:56,729 --> 00:14:59,940
Couldn't you have fallen in love
with someone else?

200
00:15:01,692 --> 00:15:06,864
Someone whose life wasn't so complicated.

201
00:15:08,991 --> 00:15:11,869
But if there's one thing
I've learned in this world…

202
00:15:13,162 --> 00:15:16,332
It's that you can't tell your heart
who to love.

203
00:15:20,252 --> 00:15:21,670
When you love,

204
00:15:23,172 --> 00:15:24,465
you love completely.

205
00:15:25,174 --> 00:15:27,968
No ifs or buts. You just love.

206
00:15:31,931 --> 00:15:33,599
That's why I'm so proud of you.

207
00:15:37,061 --> 00:15:40,773
All you wanted was someone to love.

208
00:15:41,523 --> 00:15:44,109
You never imagined

209
00:15:45,027 --> 00:15:46,862
you'd end up
in such a complicated situation.

210
00:15:50,574 --> 00:15:52,117
But you accepted the challenge.

211
00:15:52,618 --> 00:15:53,911
You found a way.

212
00:15:56,872 --> 00:15:58,374
You made it through everything.

213
00:16:04,254 --> 00:16:08,008
You fell in love,
but you never lost your way.

214
00:16:08,884 --> 00:16:11,011
I'd like to think that's because

215
00:16:11,679 --> 00:16:13,347
you were raised well.

216
00:16:16,183 --> 00:16:18,227
Well, of course, Dad!

217
00:16:18,310 --> 00:16:20,729
If it weren't for you and Mom,

218
00:16:21,438 --> 00:16:24,650
I'd probably have gone completely astray.

219
00:16:26,694 --> 00:16:27,653
Maybe.

220
00:16:29,154 --> 00:16:30,823
But I'm confident.

221
00:16:31,407 --> 00:16:32,741
I truly believe…

222
00:16:35,619 --> 00:16:37,955
wherever life takes you,

223
00:16:38,914 --> 00:16:41,417
you can handle whatever
fate throws your way.

224
00:16:46,630 --> 00:16:47,840
Thank you, Dad.

225
00:16:52,011 --> 00:16:53,512
But actually, Dad,

226
00:16:54,430 --> 00:16:57,099
I learned something
from everything I've been through.

227
00:17:01,311 --> 00:17:02,146
What's that?

228
00:17:03,981 --> 00:17:06,525
That my dad is the coolest

229
00:17:06,608 --> 00:17:09,903
and the greatest dad
in the whole wide world!

230
00:17:11,447 --> 00:17:12,865
The best!

231
00:17:15,284 --> 00:17:16,243
Hey…

232
00:17:16,326 --> 00:17:18,746
You're flattering me
like you're trying to date me.

233
00:17:22,207 --> 00:17:24,001
- Love you, Dad.
- Love you too, son.

234
00:17:30,132 --> 00:17:33,093
Chiara!

235
00:17:41,435 --> 00:17:42,519
Alex!

236
00:17:45,564 --> 00:17:46,565
Alex.

237
00:17:47,691 --> 00:17:49,151
Yes? What's wrong?

238
00:17:49,985 --> 00:17:53,280
Why don't you join Sean and me for dinner?

239
00:17:57,326 --> 00:17:59,036
"Sianong" just sounds weird.

240
00:18:02,748 --> 00:18:04,374
I'm sorry.

241
00:18:04,458 --> 00:18:06,502
I didn't know you guys were on a date.

242
00:18:06,585 --> 00:18:08,087
Let's make it a group date!

243
00:18:08,670 --> 00:18:10,422
Their paella is really good.

244
00:18:11,256 --> 00:18:13,550
It's okay, Carlota. I should get going.

245
00:18:14,843 --> 00:18:16,970
I'll see you at the office on Monday.

246
00:18:19,014 --> 00:18:20,015
But Alex…

247
00:18:22,226 --> 00:18:23,769
We're okay, right?

248
00:18:23,852 --> 00:18:26,021
There's no problem between us?

249
00:18:26,772 --> 00:18:28,857
Why would there be a problem?

250
00:18:31,944 --> 00:18:34,613
You both know how to make
your own decisions.

251
00:18:38,367 --> 00:18:39,326
What about me?

252
00:18:39,868 --> 00:18:42,246
Everybody knows who you like.

253
00:18:48,252 --> 00:18:49,294
you're right.

254
00:18:52,673 --> 00:18:56,426
We're capable of making
our own choices in life.

255
00:19:02,683 --> 00:19:04,852
I just don't want the day to come

256
00:19:05,352 --> 00:19:07,187
when you regret your choice.

257
00:19:08,230 --> 00:19:11,191
Because you never told anyone
how you truly felt.

258
00:19:13,026 --> 00:19:14,027
And Alex…

259
00:19:16,530 --> 00:19:17,364
look,

260
00:19:18,115 --> 00:19:19,491
I don't mean to interfere.

261
00:19:20,075 --> 00:19:21,285
But look at me.

262
00:19:22,327 --> 00:19:26,498
Even though I wasn't completely sure
about Mr. Sean Salindong,

263
00:19:27,332 --> 00:19:29,418
I still opened my heart.

264
00:19:30,627 --> 00:19:33,589
Because who knows?

265
00:19:33,672 --> 00:19:35,257
Maybe,

266
00:19:36,550 --> 00:19:39,261
after everything I've been through,

267
00:19:41,305 --> 00:19:44,266
I still found my happily ever after.

268
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:35,692
<i>You're right.</i>

269
00:20:39,154 --> 00:20:42,866
<i>We're capable of making decisions</i>
<i>for our own lives.</i>

270
00:20:49,706 --> 00:20:51,875
<i>I just don't want the day to come</i>

271
00:20:52,376 --> 00:20:54,336
<i>when you regret your decision</i>

272
00:20:55,254 --> 00:20:58,173
<i>because you never told anyone</i>
<i>how you truly felt.</i>

273
00:21:03,303 --> 00:21:04,721
I probably will regret it.

274
00:21:06,848 --> 00:21:08,183
But why do you care?

275
00:21:11,019 --> 00:21:13,313
I'm the one who'll regret it, not you.

276
00:21:18,026 --> 00:21:19,361
Is it really that easy?

277
00:21:22,531 --> 00:21:25,492
Is it really that easy
to tell someone how you feel?

278
00:21:28,078 --> 00:21:30,247
Is it really that easy to open your heart?

279
00:21:32,499 --> 00:21:33,875
Especially mine.

280
00:21:36,253 --> 00:21:39,381
It's so obvious that she's
head over heels in love,

281
00:21:39,464 --> 00:21:42,551
completely crazy about someone else.

282
00:21:56,023 --> 00:21:57,774
So what do you have to lose?

283
00:21:58,567 --> 00:22:01,653
What's so wrong about letting him know
how you really feel?

284
00:22:02,237 --> 00:22:04,114
You're not expecting him to love you back.

285
00:22:05,282 --> 00:22:06,700
You're not stealing him away.

286
00:22:06,783 --> 00:22:10,954
At least you won't have to keep it
bottled up inside.

287
00:22:12,122 --> 00:22:16,168
Sometimes it's better to tell the truth

288
00:22:16,251 --> 00:22:19,880
than to keep living a lie.

289
00:22:24,801 --> 00:22:26,094
You know what? You're right.

290
00:22:26,178 --> 00:22:27,846
- See?
- All right.

291
00:22:28,346 --> 00:22:30,307
- I'll take your challenge.
- That's the spirit.

292
00:22:30,390 --> 00:22:31,391
Let's drink to that.

293
00:22:32,893 --> 00:22:34,061
Who are you?

294
00:22:34,144 --> 00:22:36,146
- Where did you come from?
- I'm drinking here.

295
00:23:30,534 --> 00:23:31,910
You can do this, Alex.

296
00:23:36,414 --> 00:23:37,666
Like that.

297
00:23:48,009 --> 00:23:49,302
Is that a new dance move?

298
00:23:49,386 --> 00:23:50,762
Oh, no…

299
00:23:50,846 --> 00:23:52,848
- Someone's calling.
- Okay.

300
00:23:53,932 --> 00:23:55,392
I’ll just answer this.

301
00:23:59,354 --> 00:24:01,565
Hey, how are you? Is something wrong?

302
00:24:04,067 --> 00:24:05,360
Nothing.

303
00:24:06,862 --> 00:24:09,072
Wait. Are you checking up on me?

304
00:24:09,698 --> 00:24:11,324
Wait. You're missing me again, right?

305
00:24:13,201 --> 00:24:16,580
Actually, it's a good thing you called.
There's something I want to tell you.

306
00:24:18,957 --> 00:24:20,250
But before you do,

307
00:24:21,001 --> 00:24:22,002
let me go first.

308
00:24:23,628 --> 00:24:24,963
All right, go ahead.

309
00:24:25,589 --> 00:24:27,883
By the way, why did you call?

310
00:24:32,012 --> 00:24:33,180
Mikoy…

311
00:24:36,975 --> 00:24:38,810
I just want to tell you…

312
00:24:47,152 --> 00:24:48,695
I want you to know…

313
00:24:50,906 --> 00:24:52,032
I like you.

314
00:25:06,588 --> 00:25:08,840
I have feelings for you.

315
00:25:12,427 --> 00:25:13,970
I think I've fallen in love with you.

316
00:25:17,057 --> 00:25:19,100
<i>About that joke you made earlier…</i>

317
00:25:19,184 --> 00:25:22,145
When you said you missed me.

318
00:25:24,481 --> 00:25:26,191
My answer wasn't a joke.

319
00:25:30,362 --> 00:25:31,738
I really, really miss you.

320
00:25:35,784 --> 00:25:36,826
Alex?

321
00:25:38,036 --> 00:25:38,870
Hey!

322
00:25:43,708 --> 00:25:45,377
Did you miss us?

323
00:25:45,460 --> 00:25:47,545
Did you miss your little headaches?

324
00:25:47,629 --> 00:25:51,883
Because I missed you.
To be fair, I really missed Agent Alex.

325
00:25:52,384 --> 00:25:54,761
Should we tell her, sweetheart?

326
00:25:54,844 --> 00:25:57,222
Maybe next time, sweetheart.

327
00:25:57,305 --> 00:25:59,391
We have good news.

328
00:26:03,645 --> 00:26:05,313
Let's say it together, in…

329
00:26:05,397 --> 00:26:07,482
one, two, three…

330
00:26:07,565 --> 00:26:09,776
We're getting married!

331
00:26:09,859 --> 00:26:11,152
See? There you go.

332
00:26:26,501 --> 00:26:29,170
Everything's fine, sweetheart.
Nothing happened, okay?

333
00:26:29,254 --> 00:26:31,840
Why do I feel like that's not all I did?

334
00:26:39,723 --> 00:26:42,434
The best advice I can give you right now

335
00:26:42,517 --> 00:26:45,103
<i>is to make Mikoy and Chiara an offer.</i>

336
00:26:45,186 --> 00:26:48,481
But this isn't the right time
to bring it up with them.

337
00:26:49,441 --> 00:26:50,734
Why?

338
00:26:51,359 --> 00:26:52,944
<i>Wait. What are you doing here?</i>

339
00:26:53,028 --> 00:26:55,613
- Don't you have class?
- I just wanted to hang out with you.

340
00:26:58,033 --> 00:27:00,410
Wait… Hold on. Do you like me?

341
00:27:05,373 --> 00:27:06,875
Is something wrong, sir?

342
00:27:06,958 --> 00:27:09,502
Why would Senator Quintin want to do that?

343
00:27:09,586 --> 00:27:12,172
<i>There's no reason</i>
<i>to recruit Mikoy and Chiara.</i>

344
00:27:14,924 --> 00:27:18,219
Unless they want to form a kill squad.

345
00:27:18,303 --> 00:27:21,306
Who are they planning to eliminate?
